    "body": "### Motivation\n\nThis PR introduces `contrib/pq-shield`, an experimental standalone toolset\nimplementing the NIST FIPS 204 ML-DSA-65 post-quantum signature scheme\n(CRYSTALS-Dilithium Mode 3 equivalent) via [liboqs](https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs).\n\nA cryptographically relevant quantum computer (CRQC) running Shor's algorithm\nwould break ECDSA/secp256k1 signatures that secure Bitcoin transactions.\nWhile CRQCs do not exist today, the Bitcoin Core project should have\nexperimental infrastructure ready to evaluate post-quantum signature schemes\nwell before any migration becomes necessary.\n\nThis tool is **additive only** — no consensus changes, no wallet integration,\nno P2P changes. It lives entirely in `contrib/` for developers and researchers\nto experiment with ML-DSA-65 key generation, signing, verification, and key\nauditing.\n\n### Technical approach\n\n- **Algorithm**: ML-DSA-65 (NIST FIPS 204, security level 3 ≈ AES-192)\n- **Library**: liboqs (C library, MIT/BSD licensed, constant-time implementations)\n- **Language**: C++20, integrates with Bitcoin Core's CMake build system\n- **Components**:\n  - `pq-shield`: CLI for keygen/sign/verify\n  - `pq-shield-audit`: validates key sizes and enforces 0600 permissions on private keys\n  - `test-pq-shield`: ctest suite (round-trip, tamper resistance, permission checks)\n\n### Testing\n\n- Unit tests cover key generation, signing round-trip, tamper resistance, and file permission auditing\n- All tests pass locally on Linux with liboqs built with `Sig:Ml-Dsa*`\n- Build verified with CMake 3.16+\n\n### Security considerations\n\n- Private keys written with mode `0600`; audit tool rejects looser modes\n- ML-DSA-65 signatures are ~3.3 KB, public keys ~1.9 KB (10-20× ECDSA)\n- Constant-time liboqs implementations mitigate side-channel risk\n- No consensus changes — this is purely an experimental tool in `contrib/`\n\n### Build instructions\n\nSee `contrib/pq-shield/README.md` for full build steps. In summary:\n\n```sh\n# Build liboqs with ML-DSA only (minimal)\ngit clone --depth 1 https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\ncmake -S liboqs -B liboqs/build -DOQS_BUILD_ONLY_LIB=ON -DOQS_MINIMAL_BUILD=\"Sig:Ml-Dsa*\"\ncmake --build liboqs/build\n\n# Build pq-shield\ncmake -S contrib/pq-shield -B build/pq-shield -DLIBOQS_ROOT=$PWD/liboqs/build\ncmake --build build/pq-shield\n\n# Run tests\nctest --test-dir build/pq-shield\n```\n\n### References\n\n- NIST FIPS 204: https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/final\n- liboqs: https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\n- Bitcoin Core post-quantum discussions: various mailing list threads\n\n---\n\n**Note**: This PR replaces previously closed attempts (#34607, #36423) which\nwere auto-closed due to incomplete PR metadata and references to a non-existent\n\"PIP-2030\" (Bitcoin uses BIPs, not PIPs). This submission follows\nCONTRIBUTING.md guidelines with complete title, description, and scope.\n",
